In XX/XX/2016 I called in to the call center to see why my minimum payment had increased. One of the agents told me I was late paying more than two times in a calendar year and the interest rate had increased. I asked him to lower it back down, and I will continue my monthly payments. He said he can not change it because it is in the agreement that I signed. So I ask to get a copy of the contract that I signed. The agent said " you have to request the copy of the contract in writing '' and gave me the following address : CapitalOne - Department General Correspondence, XXXX. I sent a written request and I did not get copy of the contract. 
I have a charge-off on my credit report and I never got what I asked for, a copy of the contract before it went into default. 
